label job
Ben: Actually, glad you came by. I've got a job for you.
- What kind of job?
	Ben: The Fuel Stop on Main Street. This time of night, that register's full.
	John: You want me to rob the gas station?
	Ben: Just bring me the money. All of it. I'll make it worth your while.
	- Sure, I'm in.
		[signal arg="accept"]
		Ben: That's my guy! I knew I could count on you.
		Ben: Go on. I'll be right here.
	- Not tonight, Ben.
		[signal arg="reject"]
		Ben: No worries. The offer stands.
		Ben: Knock if you change your mind.
	- Why don't you do it yourself?
		[signal arg="cold"]
		Ben: Me? Oh, John. Some of us have reputations to keep.
		Ben: Not everyone gets to just... be you.
		- Fine. I'll do it.
			[signal arg="accept"]
			Ben: Wow. Thank you SO much. I'm touched. Really.
		- Nah. Forget it.
			[signal arg="reject"]
			Ben: No, no, it's fine. I'll just sit here. Broke. Alone.
			Ben: Don't worry about me. You never do.
- Make it quick, Ben. My beer's getting warm.
	[signal arg="cold"]
	Ben: Lovely to see you too, John.
	Ben: The Fuel Stop on Main Street. Rob it. Bring me the money. Is that quick enough for you?
	- Fine. I'll do it.
		[signal arg="accept"]
		Ben: Look at you, helping out a friend. I'll mark the calendar.
	- Not interested.
		[signal arg="reject"]
		Ben: Of course you're not. Go enjoy your warm beer, John.
[end_timeline]

label again_nice
Ben: Hey, John. Change your mind about that job?
- Yeah. I'll do it.
	[signal arg="accept"]
	Ben: Knew you'd come around. Fuel Stop. Register. All of it.
- Still no.
	[signal arg="reject"]
	Ben: Alright, alright. You know where I live.
- Why don't you just do it yourself?
	[signal arg="cold"]
	[signal arg="reject"]
	Ben: Wow. Okay. Forget I asked.
[end_timeline]

label again_cold
Ben: Oh. It's you. Here to let me down again?
- Fine. I'll do the job.
	[signal arg="accept"]
	Ben: Well, well. Miracles do happen.
- Sorry about before. I'm in.
	[signal arg="nice"]
	[signal arg="accept"]
	Ben: ...Apology accepted. Now go. Fuel Stop. All of it.
- Just came to say hi.
	[signal arg="reject"]
	Ben: How thoughtful. Hi, John. Bye, John.
[end_timeline]

label remind_nice
Ben: Fuel Stop. Register. Money. You've got this, John.
[end_timeline]

label remind_cold
Ben: The register isn't going to empty itself, John.
Ben: Take your time. It's not like I'm waiting or anything.
[end_timeline]

label already
Ben: Hold on. Is that a wad of cash in your pocket?
John: Might be. The Fuel Stop had a bad night.
Ben: Ha! You beat me to it. I was going to ask you to do exactly that.
Ben: Hand it over and I'll cut you in.
- Here. Take it.
	[signal arg="owed"]
	jump pay_nice
- Get your own.
	[signal arg="cold"]
	[signal arg="reject"]
	Ben: Wow. Okay. Enjoy your money, I guess.
[end_timeline]

label pay_nice
John: Here. All of it.
Ben: Ha! Look at that! You beautiful lunatic.
[signal arg="paid"]
Ben: There's your cut. Now get lost before the cops come knocking.
[end_timeline]

label pay_cold
John: Here. All of it.
Ben: Huh. You actually did it. I'm almost proud.
[signal arg="paid"]
Ben: There's your cut. Don't spend it all on beer. Who am I kidding.
[end_timeline]

label pay_short
John: Here. That's... most of it.
Ben: That's it? Where's the rest of it, John?
[signal arg="paid"]
Ben: Whatever. There's your cut. Next time, don't stop for snacks.
[end_timeline]

label after_nice
Ben: Lay low for a while, John. We're square.
[end_timeline]

label after_cold
Ben: We're square. Don't let the door hit you on the way out.
[end_timeline]
